# A field that is only stepped by one, in functions that compare it or read it as a key, is an exact integer and lies in a slot of integers. Sums, products, fractions and counters that are only told stay numbers.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.0 "up" proven=int[0, 9007199254740992] writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.1 "both" proven=int[-9007199254740992, 9007199254740992] writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.2 "sum" proven=number writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.3 "twice" proven=number writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.4 "mixed" proven=number writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.5 "last" proven=int[0, 9007199254740992] writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.6 "told" proven=number writers-known
# CHECK: field L0.7 "key" proven=int[0, 9007199254740992] writers-known
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: 4 0 10 15 0.9375 4 4 abcundefined
